# Licence

This repository is dual-licensed. The prose and the code are covered
separately, because they are used in different ways.

## The book

Everything under `book/`, and the HTML and PDF built from it, is licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
(CC BY-SA 4.0).

    Git by Example: A Complete Offline Handbook
    Copyright (c) 2026 M. Reza Norouzi
    Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0

In short, you may copy it, print it, put it on a phone and hand it to somebody
with no internet, translate it, and build on it, including commercially, as
long as you credit the author and license what you build on it under the same
terms.

The full legal text is at <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode>
and a plain-language summary is at <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>.

## The code

Everything under `sandbox/` and `tools/`, which is the harness that generates
the examples and the scripts that build the book, is licensed under the MIT
licence. The example scripts exist to be copied and adapted, so they carry no
share-alike obligation.

